WEBVTT

01:49.109 --> 01:56.116
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

02:17.929 --> 02:20.932
ALL TROOPS RETREAT

02:28.106 --> 02:31.234
Finish all preparations
to retreat within 48 hours.

02:31.860 --> 02:35.029
Take all the documents
and research records back to Japan,

02:35.738 --> 02:39.325
and incinerate everything
that cannot be taken.

02:39.868 --> 02:40.952
Yes, sir!

02:47.876 --> 02:49.085
Are we to burn

02:49.919 --> 02:51.254
everything, sir?

02:51.337 --> 02:52.797
Burn everything.

02:53.506 --> 02:55.383
Do not leave a single trace

02:56.426 --> 02:57.802
of what we did here.

02:58.761 --> 02:59.721
That'll be all.

03:07.020 --> 03:08.104
Quickly!

03:08.188 --> 03:10.064
Destroy everything. There's no time!

03:10.148 --> 03:11.107
Hurry up!

03:13.067 --> 03:14.986
- On your feet!
- Yes, sir!

03:15.069 --> 03:17.405
- Leave no evidence. Take this.
- No time!

04:01.824 --> 04:02.742
All planted, sir.

04:02.825 --> 04:03.868
- Over there!
- Okay!

04:15.088 --> 04:17.257
- The serums?
- We have secured 12, sir.

04:17.340 --> 04:19.342
- And the Najin?
- We have eight of them.

04:19.425 --> 04:21.219
What about the other two?

04:21.302 --> 04:23.554
We didn't have enough time
to retrieve them.

04:35.858 --> 04:37.193
Lieutenant Colonel Kato!

04:45.118 --> 04:47.745
There is not enough time. Please hurry!

05:30.538 --> 05:31.539
Ready!

05:34.459 --> 05:35.460
Fire!

05:45.386 --> 05:46.220
Fire!

05:49.474 --> 05:50.350
Fire!

05:54.479 --> 05:56.022
Faster!

05:58.441 --> 05:59.317
Hurry.

06:01.694 --> 06:03.488
What are you doing? Hurry up!

06:44.570 --> 06:46.322
Come on! There's no time!

06:47.365 --> 06:48.199
Are we flying?

06:48.282 --> 06:50.785
Traveling by land
seems to be the safest path right now.

06:50.868 --> 06:53.579
We'll take the train at Harbin
and go to Gyeongseong first.

06:54.539 --> 06:55.790
- Drive.
- Yes, sir.

07:46.174 --> 07:49.552
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN GOOD AND EVIL

07:49.635 --> 07:52.180
EPISODE 1
NAJIN

08:00.188 --> 08:01.981
LATE MARCH, 1945
GYEONGSEONG (OLD SEOUL)

08:02.064 --> 08:05.485
Spring was on its way to Gyeongseong
unusually quickly that year.

08:38.309 --> 08:39.644
Get your papers!

08:39.727 --> 08:40.811
Shoeshine!

08:41.437 --> 08:43.064
- Papers!
- Shoeshine!

08:43.147 --> 08:44.482
- Papers!
- Kid!

08:46.067 --> 08:47.068
Thank you.

08:48.194 --> 08:50.530
Boy, I'll take one.

08:53.115 --> 08:53.950
One jeon.

08:58.454 --> 09:00.456
Get yourself some bread with the change.

09:00.540 --> 09:02.208
Thank you, sir!

09:02.291 --> 09:03.626
May you be blessed.

09:07.797 --> 09:09.006
Tell you what,

09:10.049 --> 09:11.634
this here is the real news.

09:14.387 --> 09:16.264
Papers!

09:16.347 --> 09:18.349
JAPAN'S CRISIS!
LARGE-SCALE AIR RAIDS WRECK TOKYO

09:18.432 --> 09:20.393
So the rumors were true.

09:21.435 --> 09:23.646
After the Bombing of Tokyo on March 9,

09:24.272 --> 09:26.607
the shadow of defeat loomed over Japan.

09:27.358 --> 09:32.446
In the hopes that Japan may fall,
Joseon was quivering in silence.

09:32.530 --> 09:33.531
However…

09:38.202 --> 09:40.371
Insurgents! Arrest them all!

09:41.330 --> 09:42.748
Get them!

09:47.378 --> 09:48.337
Don't move!

09:51.424 --> 09:52.842
Arrest them all!

09:52.925 --> 09:53.843
Let's go.

09:59.432 --> 10:02.435
JAPAN'S CRISIS!
LARGE-SCALE AIR RAIDS WRECK TOYKO

10:05.605 --> 10:07.189
- Run!
- What is it?

10:07.273 --> 10:08.274
Who is it?

10:29.128 --> 10:31.213
People of the peninsula, rise!

10:32.089 --> 10:34.717
It's your chance
to give your life for His Majesty!

10:35.760 --> 10:40.264
Join the unbeatable Imperial Army
and enter the shrine of Yasukuni!

10:44.018 --> 10:45.978
Either die in a torture chamber…

10:48.898 --> 10:50.650
or become an honorable soldier.

10:54.195 --> 10:55.363
Make your choice.

10:57.948 --> 11:00.743
Damn it, what do I do?

11:03.829 --> 11:06.749
CONSCRIPTION FORM

11:06.832 --> 11:08.501
You know what they say.

11:09.543 --> 11:11.379
It's always darkest before the dawn.

11:24.809 --> 11:25.935
Admit it.

11:26.936 --> 11:29.522
It… wasn't me.

11:30.272 --> 11:32.858
So, you're going to keep denying it?

11:33.442 --> 11:34.610
I swear…

11:36.862 --> 11:38.030
I don't know anything.

11:48.874 --> 11:50.584
Is he part of the independence army?

11:50.668 --> 11:52.294
You don't know who he is?

11:53.337 --> 11:54.547
That's Jang Tae-sang.

11:55.673 --> 11:58.008
Jang Tae-sang? Who's that?

11:58.092 --> 12:00.219
The master
of the House of Golden Treasure.

12:01.345 --> 12:02.430
Golden Treasure?

12:03.973 --> 12:06.100
That's right.
The House of Golden Treasure.

12:06.976 --> 12:10.312
Located in the corner
that is the prime spot of Bonjeong,

12:10.396 --> 12:11.564
it is, without a doubt,

12:11.647 --> 12:15.568
Gyeongseong's largest
and finest establishment.

12:15.651 --> 12:18.446
Yes, it's that pawnshop
that everyone is talking about.

12:20.698 --> 12:22.992
It's the famous Waltham watches.

12:24.118 --> 12:25.119
Four won, 50 jeon.

12:25.202 --> 12:26.287
Hey!

12:26.370 --> 12:29.457
This Waltham watch came
all the way from America!

12:29.540 --> 12:30.791
Four won, 50 jeon.

12:34.044 --> 12:35.296
Look.

12:35.379 --> 12:38.716
I've lost my factory to the Japanese.

12:38.799 --> 12:40.634
- I might lose my house too.
- Oh dear.

12:40.718 --> 12:44.054
I have an elderly mother
and four little ones to provide for.

12:44.138 --> 12:46.474
And we're about to end up on the streets…

12:46.557 --> 12:47.391
Here.

12:47.475 --> 12:51.771
That's one more won for you.
Take the money or take the watch back.

12:55.900 --> 12:57.067
Next!

12:57.818 --> 13:00.821
These are my dowries.
Please take good care of them.

13:00.905 --> 13:03.824
I will come back for them, no matter what.

13:03.908 --> 13:05.576
Fifteen won for the batch.

13:06.285 --> 13:08.370
For the record, this one's a fake.

13:08.454 --> 13:09.997
An Italian suit.

13:10.080 --> 13:11.874
I had it custom-made at a shop…

13:11.957 --> 13:13.501
Two won for used clothes.

13:14.585 --> 13:17.838
I paid quite a lot for this baekja
three years ago.

13:17.922 --> 13:19.965
Oh, is that so?

13:21.175 --> 13:22.343
Take it back.

13:22.426 --> 13:23.928
It's a chamber pot.

13:25.471 --> 13:26.764
Stupid man.

13:54.166 --> 13:56.335
- What do you mean?
- Kid.

14:08.597 --> 14:10.808
Try stealing from the shop one more time,

14:11.392 --> 14:13.936
I'll cut off all ten of your fingers.

14:14.019 --> 14:17.773
It was just a little prank.
Don't be so harsh!

15:04.778 --> 15:06.405
We don't get Walthams often.

15:07.907 --> 15:12.036
Four won would have been enough,
but he gave five won and 50 jeon for it.

15:12.703 --> 15:16.749
Manager Gu is being too generous
with money that isn't his.

15:17.416 --> 15:18.500
This is good leather.

15:19.335 --> 15:20.419
It's worth the price.

15:21.170 --> 15:23.255
Beom-o, that kid, is also hopeless.

15:23.964 --> 15:27.384
The little brat tries to swipe things
every chance he gets.

15:27.468 --> 15:31.722
Have you prepared the tea set and tray
for Lady Maeda?

15:32.806 --> 15:36.769
They say that one should avoid bad company
for their own good.

15:37.269 --> 15:40.856
Her husband is Ishikawa,
and her father is General Maeda.

15:41.357 --> 15:44.818
Her family has this city
in the palm of their hands.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.488
Of course I should keep them close, dear.

15:49.406 --> 15:50.824
Still, you should be careful.

15:51.700 --> 15:52.785
Not to worry.

15:53.535 --> 15:54.453
I'm

15:55.371 --> 15:56.538
Jang Tae-sang.

15:57.957 --> 16:00.292
That's right. I'm Jang Tae-sang.

16:01.168 --> 16:04.088
A man of means in Bukchon
and an icon of a self-made man.

16:09.301 --> 16:10.886
Oh my goodness!

16:12.304 --> 16:14.306
- Greetings, everyone.
- Master Jang!

16:14.390 --> 16:15.557
Calm yourselves.

16:16.141 --> 16:17.476
One, two!

16:17.977 --> 16:19.687
- Good! One more!
- A different pose?

16:31.448 --> 16:32.616
Mr. Jang!

16:32.700 --> 16:33.784
Hey!

16:33.867 --> 16:36.245
Nothing scares me. Nothing can stop me.

16:36.328 --> 16:40.082
I'm the master of Golden Treasure,
and I can get anything I want.

16:40.165 --> 16:41.667
Everyone. Cheers!

16:41.750 --> 16:43.502
Cheers!

16:44.461 --> 16:46.255
The one and only Jang Tae-sang.

16:48.173 --> 16:49.008
So…

17:00.102 --> 17:02.730
how did I end up in this sorry mess?

17:03.355 --> 17:06.150
He must have secretly funded
the independence movement.

17:06.233 --> 17:07.401
Wrong.

17:07.484 --> 17:09.319
Then was he a spy?

17:09.862 --> 17:10.779
Nope.

17:15.034 --> 17:16.118
It was an affair.

17:17.202 --> 17:18.203
An affair?

17:20.289 --> 17:23.876
Why did you meet her at a teahouse
about a month ago?

17:25.127 --> 17:30.758
Lady Maeda was looking for baekja teacups
and a lacquered tray inlaid with nacre.

17:30.841 --> 17:32.760
What about at the museum six days ago?

17:32.843 --> 17:37.973
To tell her that it's not easy to acquire
baekja teacups and lacquered trays.

17:38.057 --> 17:40.142
You sent her a message three days ago.

17:40.225 --> 17:44.229
Because I had a stroke of luck
and was able to find

17:45.022 --> 17:46.440
the teacups and the tray.

17:46.523 --> 17:48.692
You even came to my house yesterday.

17:48.776 --> 17:50.861
I had gone through a lot to get them, so…

17:53.030 --> 17:54.281
I delivered them in person.

17:54.364 --> 17:55.491
Don't mess with me!

17:57.451 --> 18:00.746
You pathetic, inferior Josenjing bastard!

18:00.829 --> 18:04.208
How dare you covet my wife?

18:07.377 --> 18:13.008
It seems to me, Commissioner,
that there is a misunderstanding.

18:15.177 --> 18:17.137
Cut the bullshit and spit it out.

18:18.263 --> 18:23.102
What the hell did you do with my wife?
Tell me now!

18:28.524 --> 18:30.150
You must be crazy…

18:32.111 --> 18:34.947
crazily in love, Commissioner Ishikawa!

18:35.656 --> 18:39.409
Don't tell me you're seriously
suspecting your own wife.

18:40.619 --> 18:44.456
How could you doubt an honorable
and noble woman like Lady Maeda?

18:44.540 --> 18:45.707
I must definitely say

18:46.542 --> 18:49.461
that this is a great affront
and insult to her.

18:49.545 --> 18:50.796
What are you saying?

18:50.879 --> 18:54.007
Would it be okay with you
if Lady Maeda found out

18:55.509 --> 18:58.428
that you were doubting her faithfulness?

18:59.179 --> 19:00.013
That's what.

19:37.593 --> 19:41.430
Now, why don't we move on
to the actual matter at hand?

19:42.890 --> 19:44.641
What do you actually want from me?

19:49.605 --> 19:51.273
This girl has gone missing.

19:53.525 --> 19:56.320
It's been about a week now.

20:00.616 --> 20:02.326
A missing persons case?

20:03.702 --> 20:05.704
Sounds like a job for the police.

20:05.787 --> 20:07.998
They say you're Mr. Omniscient.

20:08.874 --> 20:10.125
You flatter me.

20:10.209 --> 20:14.213
"You must go through Jang Tae-sang
if you want anything in Bonjeong,

20:14.296 --> 20:17.299
whether it be money,
property, or a person."

20:18.550 --> 20:19.384
Is that not true?

20:19.468 --> 20:22.137
I catch those who don't pay me back,

20:23.805 --> 20:24.973
not courtesans.

20:30.687 --> 20:32.522
Find the girl.

20:33.690 --> 20:37.486
Find out why she's vanished, where she is,
and if she found a lover to elope with.

20:37.569 --> 20:40.489
If she did, then find him as well.

20:42.282 --> 20:45.786
If you fail to find her…

20:47.663 --> 20:48.580
Will I die?

20:53.543 --> 20:56.213
You will lose everything you own.

20:57.506 --> 20:59.424
From the house that you own,

20:59.508 --> 21:04.263
to real estate, cash, cars, and even
the House of Golden Treasure in Bonjeong!

21:05.639 --> 21:06.974
You'll lose them all.

21:07.057 --> 21:08.225
And as for you?

21:09.768 --> 21:11.311
You will be sent to war.

21:34.334 --> 21:36.253
How much time do I have?

21:39.214 --> 21:42.384
Until the cherry blossoms fall.

21:49.891 --> 21:50.892
I see.

21:53.812 --> 21:54.896
Okay, sir.

22:11.079 --> 22:11.997
Sir!

22:30.557 --> 22:33.226
What is the matter?

22:36.188 --> 22:37.981
Who beat the crap out of you?

22:39.775 --> 22:40.859
Mrs. Nawol.

22:41.777 --> 22:44.112
How much cash
do we have on hand right now?

22:45.364 --> 22:46.406
Cash?

22:49.284 --> 22:51.286
If I put my buildings in Bukchon,

22:51.870 --> 22:54.164
my house, and this shop
up for urgent sale,

22:54.915 --> 22:57.167
how long would it take for them to sell?

23:03.256 --> 23:04.758
Maybe a month?

23:06.551 --> 23:08.303
What's going on this time?

23:08.845 --> 23:10.013
Tell me, will you?

23:18.397 --> 23:19.564
You know what?

23:20.732 --> 23:21.650
It seems…

23:25.153 --> 23:26.321
I'm screwed.

23:32.119 --> 23:33.370
What is all this?

23:33.453 --> 23:34.663
Look at the yeot!

23:36.164 --> 23:37.582
It looks so good.

23:38.166 --> 23:41.002
He's making that sound
with the scissors so well!

23:44.798 --> 23:45.882
Wait here.

23:57.477 --> 23:58.728
Excuse me.

24:00.021 --> 24:02.023
We haven't opened yet.

24:06.820 --> 24:08.738
I'm looking for someone.

24:10.657 --> 24:15.495
Do you know a Japanese man named Sachimoto
who frequents this shop?

24:17.622 --> 24:20.083
I heard that he was a painter.

24:20.167 --> 24:23.837
I've known two Sachimotos in my life,

24:24.880 --> 24:27.382
but they were both soldiers, not painters.

24:29.134 --> 24:30.802
I heard he was a regular here.

24:31.386 --> 24:32.554
I'm not sure.

24:32.637 --> 24:35.807
I've been working here
for almost six months now,

24:35.891 --> 24:37.726
but I haven't met such a man.

24:38.894 --> 24:39.895
I see.

24:41.730 --> 24:44.149
Why don't you try
the House of Golden Treasure?

24:45.734 --> 24:49.321
Master Jang Tae-sang runs the place.

24:49.905 --> 24:53.992
They say you must go through him
if you want anything in Bonjeong,

24:54.659 --> 24:58.497
whether it be money,
property, or a person.

24:59.247 --> 25:01.791
He's Mr. Omniscient of Gyeongseong.

25:02.918 --> 25:03.752
What was that?

25:03.835 --> 25:06.796
I asked if that thing outside
was for sale.

25:08.590 --> 25:10.050
Oh, that?

25:11.176 --> 25:13.887
It's broken. The engine's busted.

25:13.970 --> 25:16.723
I'll buy it. How much do you want?

25:19.518 --> 25:23.522
Judging by your appearance,
you must be from Manchuria, right?

25:23.605 --> 25:25.315
- Say, 200 won?
- Hey!

25:25.398 --> 25:27.484
It has a sidecar and everything.

25:27.567 --> 25:28.568
Make it 300 won!

25:29.319 --> 25:30.779
You said it was broken.

25:32.072 --> 25:34.824
It's worthless junk
if you leave it like that.

25:34.908 --> 25:36.785
A diamond on a dunghill
is still a diamond,

25:36.868 --> 25:39.454
just as a broken motorcycle
is still a motorcycle!

25:45.210 --> 25:46.211
Fine.

25:46.795 --> 25:49.214
Make it 280 won, then.

25:51.216 --> 25:52.926
- 280?
- Yes.

26:13.530 --> 26:16.157
I will buy all of these and the bike

26:17.284 --> 26:18.535
for 250 won.

26:18.618 --> 26:20.453
I don't accept Chinese bills.

26:51.401 --> 26:53.945
Did that kid strike gold or something?

26:54.613 --> 26:57.532
My goodness!
I said it was broken, didn't I?

26:57.616 --> 27:02.495
It's been there for over three years,
weathering the hail, snow, and rain.

27:02.579 --> 27:04.581
There's no way you can get it to…

27:18.178 --> 27:20.764
Forget it! There's no need to worry.

27:20.847 --> 27:23.058
Hey. Don't look so serious.

27:23.141 --> 27:26.770
I mean, who are you?
You're Mr. Omniscient of Gyeongseong.

27:26.853 --> 27:29.856
We'll contact all your sources
and look for the girl.

27:29.939 --> 27:32.442
Where else would Myeong-ja
of Spring Moon Hall be?

27:32.525 --> 27:34.861
She probably eloped with a guy or--

27:34.944 --> 27:37.739
What man in Gyeongseong
would be stupid enough

27:38.531 --> 27:40.617
to run off with Ishikawa's girl?

27:43.161 --> 27:47.165
Wait, could this be another case
of the recent disappearances of women?

27:48.500 --> 27:51.211
It's causing quite a stir
all over Bukchon and Namchon.

27:51.836 --> 27:54.172
They keep on disappearing, you know.

27:54.923 --> 27:58.677
I've heard some horrible rumors.
What if Myeong-ja is a victim?

27:59.260 --> 28:01.846
Gosh, this is bad. Real bad.

28:01.930 --> 28:03.515
What do we do now?

28:06.768 --> 28:07.769
Master Jang,

28:08.812 --> 28:12.732
why don't we take this chance
to just sell everything and leave Joseon?

28:12.816 --> 28:15.360
I have a close friend in Osaka--

28:15.443 --> 28:17.320
Stop with the nonsense, Mr. Gu!

28:17.821 --> 28:20.824
Let me talk for once, please!

28:20.907 --> 28:24.327
Why do you shoot me down
every time I try to say something?

28:24.411 --> 28:27.330
Because you always spit out
mindless drivel. That's why.

28:27.414 --> 28:29.499
I do think before I speak, you know!

28:29.582 --> 28:31.751
I'm not as short-sighted as you think!

28:31.835 --> 28:35.922
Let's say Master Jang does put up
his real estate in a hurry.

28:36.005 --> 28:39.759
The rumors will spread like wildfire
across Gyeongseong.

28:39.843 --> 28:42.721
So what? Is that such a bad thing?

28:42.804 --> 28:44.848
Then Ishikawa will hear about it.

28:45.640 --> 28:47.183
And when he does,

28:48.351 --> 28:49.769
what would he do to Master?

28:53.690 --> 28:54.524
My bad.

28:55.817 --> 28:57.235
I didn't think it through.

29:16.337 --> 29:18.339
Ishikawa has a lot of eyes on me.

29:19.215 --> 29:21.134
- Mr. Gu.
- Yes, go on.

29:21.217 --> 29:23.970
Contact every informant
and connection we have,

29:24.053 --> 29:25.847
and look for leads on Myeong-ja.

29:26.473 --> 29:29.225
Find out whatever she did
before she went missing.

29:29.309 --> 29:30.477
All right.

29:30.560 --> 29:32.061
Sounds like a good plan.

29:32.812 --> 29:34.856
Let's do everything we can, Mrs. Nawol.

29:36.733 --> 29:37.817
Beom-o.

29:38.526 --> 29:40.904
Go and find Young Master Kwon Jun-taek.

29:40.987 --> 29:42.238
Why do you need him?

29:42.906 --> 29:45.241
He's the only man in Gyeongseong

29:45.325 --> 29:47.994
audacious enough
to mess with Ishikawa's girl.

29:48.077 --> 29:49.579
Tell him to come here.

29:49.662 --> 29:50.622
Yes, sir.

29:51.706 --> 29:53.041
Mrs. Nawol.

29:53.124 --> 29:56.544
Start selling the most expensive items
in the vault

29:57.045 --> 29:59.172
as quickly and discreetly as possible.

29:59.672 --> 30:03.134
Take gold as well as cash.
Secure as many funds as you can.

30:04.803 --> 30:08.056
And look into ships
that set sail over the next month.

30:08.723 --> 30:09.808
If need be,

30:11.684 --> 30:13.812
we might really have to leave Gyeongseong.

30:15.313 --> 30:16.314
Yes, Master.

30:41.089 --> 30:43.049
Mr. Omniscient of Gyeongseong, huh?

30:44.175 --> 30:46.261
He gets a lot of attention, indeed.

31:08.491 --> 31:10.493
Jang Tae-sang is on the move, sir.

31:10.577 --> 31:15.665
All of his employees have set out
to look for leads regarding Miss Akiko.

31:17.292 --> 31:18.376
All right.

31:19.377 --> 31:20.545
You're dismissed.

31:20.628 --> 31:21.629
Yes, sir.

31:41.649 --> 31:45.111
I think I'm pregnant.

31:47.739 --> 31:48.573
Pregnant?

31:49.532 --> 31:50.617
Yes.

31:50.700 --> 31:52.285
With your child, sir.

32:04.589 --> 32:06.132
Your wife called, sir.

32:06.215 --> 32:08.843
She wishes to know
when you will be coming home today.

32:08.927 --> 32:10.511
Tell her not to wait.

32:11.763 --> 32:14.474
I'll be very late
due to the missing persons case.

32:15.183 --> 32:17.018
Yes, sir. I'll let her know.

32:23.608 --> 32:24.525
Yes.

32:25.485 --> 32:26.694
I see.

32:27.320 --> 32:29.364
No. Yes.

32:30.865 --> 32:31.866
Bye, then.

32:44.212 --> 32:46.965
Get up, all of you. To your positions!

32:49.509 --> 32:51.511
Hurry up! Move your ass!

32:57.225 --> 32:58.726
What's happening?

32:58.810 --> 33:00.228
Don't make a sound.

33:00.728 --> 33:02.021
Keep your head down.

33:02.897 --> 33:03.731
What?

33:25.336 --> 33:26.754
Will two be enough?

33:27.547 --> 33:29.882
Yes. That will be enough for now.

33:40.018 --> 33:40.935
This one.

33:41.686 --> 33:43.187
- Take her out.
- Yes, sir.

33:47.567 --> 33:48.776
Don't kill me.

33:48.860 --> 33:50.611
Please don't kill me!

33:55.992 --> 33:57.243
Tell me about that one.

33:58.828 --> 34:02.040
We brought her
from Seodaemun Prison a while ago,

34:02.915 --> 34:04.709
but her condition is a bit…

34:06.210 --> 34:07.211
Let me see.

34:08.129 --> 34:09.881
- Take her out.
- Yes, sir.

34:42.497 --> 34:43.581
Heads down!

34:44.749 --> 34:45.917
What shall we do, sir?

34:46.000 --> 34:47.376
Please don't kill me!

34:52.632 --> 34:54.092
Don't do this.

34:59.764 --> 35:01.099
These two will do.

35:02.934 --> 35:04.519
Please don't kill me.

35:05.019 --> 35:06.854
Please don't!

35:07.647 --> 35:09.273
Please!

35:09.357 --> 35:11.234
Let me live.

35:11.317 --> 35:13.152
Please don't kill me!

35:21.953 --> 35:23.121
Don't kill me!

37:43.719 --> 37:44.553
What is it?

37:44.637 --> 37:47.765
Can you give me a ride to Bukchon?
I have to meet someone there.

37:49.100 --> 37:50.101
What?

37:50.184 --> 37:51.769
You speak the Joseon tongue.

37:52.687 --> 37:54.689
You must be bored
from watching me all day.

37:54.772 --> 37:57.775
Why don't you have some fun
by giving me a ride?

37:58.401 --> 38:01.696
You were going to tail me anyway,
so let's not make this complicated.

38:03.072 --> 38:03.990
Seriously…

38:04.073 --> 38:05.199
Hey, wait…

38:05.283 --> 38:06.867
Let us go to Bukchon.

38:12.540 --> 38:14.000
Come on. Let's go.

38:31.017 --> 38:35.187
My goodness, are you trying to empty out
the secret vault in your shop?

38:35.271 --> 38:36.814
Dear me…

38:36.897 --> 38:39.859
All the items are of the highest quality.
No need to check.

38:39.942 --> 38:43.738
Well, that goes without saying.
They're from the House of Golden Treasure.

38:45.823 --> 38:48.200
Can you get it done in ten days?

38:48.284 --> 38:50.536
Ten days? That's a bit tight.

38:53.748 --> 38:57.335
It isn't like you to rush things.
What's the hurry?

38:57.918 --> 39:01.505
Has Master Jang really decided
to leave Gyeongseong?

39:02.840 --> 39:05.343
The rumors have spread all over town!

39:05.426 --> 39:09.680
That he's in a pickle
because of Ishikawa's mistress or whatnot.

39:09.764 --> 39:13.017
Shut your trap,
or I will sew it shut for you.

39:15.311 --> 39:19.982
Actually, I'm only bringing this up
because I heard that sleuths are in town.

39:20.066 --> 39:22.651
They could be of some help to Master Jang.

39:23.861 --> 39:24.695
Sleuths?

39:24.779 --> 39:28.949
Yes, sleuths.
They're experts at finding missing people.

39:29.450 --> 39:32.536
In Manchuria, they call them sleuths.

39:33.245 --> 39:34.163
Go on.

39:34.246 --> 39:37.208
I know a friend
whose older cousin's daughter

39:37.291 --> 39:40.461
went missing for three years
after she disappeared during Dano.

39:40.544 --> 39:42.129
But then those sleuths

39:42.880 --> 39:45.549
went all the way to Southern China
and brought her back.

39:45.633 --> 39:48.552
She was forced to be a comfort girl,
but they still found her!

39:48.636 --> 39:50.304
They went to Southern China?

39:50.388 --> 39:52.723
Yeah, not to mention
every corner of Joseon.

39:52.807 --> 39:55.601
They cover Manchuria, Yanbian,
Southern China, you name it.

39:55.684 --> 39:58.687
If the person is already dead,
they bring back the bones at least.

39:59.271 --> 40:00.272
Is that right?

40:02.817 --> 40:04.693
Where can I find these sleuths?

40:28.968 --> 40:32.012
Thanks for the ride.
It was nice and comfortable.

40:40.354 --> 40:41.605
- Wait…
- Don't…

40:41.689 --> 40:42.523
Hey!

40:43.274 --> 40:44.817
Treat yourself to a meal.

40:45.734 --> 40:49.447
I won't tell Ishikawa, so just take it.

41:00.291 --> 41:01.125
What the heck?

41:15.848 --> 41:19.351
Welcome, sir! How many of you are there?

41:19.435 --> 41:21.187
I'm not here to dine.

41:21.270 --> 41:23.481
I need to pass through your back door.

41:24.398 --> 41:25.691
This way, Master Jang.

41:50.174 --> 41:53.177
IDIOT

42:37.304 --> 42:38.305
Who are you?

42:39.098 --> 42:40.516
Why are you following me?

42:44.436 --> 42:47.147
You don't seem like
one of Ishikawa's underlings.

42:47.940 --> 42:49.108
Who do you work for?

42:49.191 --> 42:51.110
Tell me who sent you here!

42:53.571 --> 42:55.030
Master Jang of Golden Treasure?

42:55.114 --> 42:57.783
It's bad manners to answer a question
with a question.

42:58.867 --> 42:59.702
Not to mention…

43:02.371 --> 43:05.040
that you're carrying
such a dangerous item.

44:38.217 --> 44:39.385
Are you here to kill me?

44:40.094 --> 44:41.929
I wasn't planning on it.

44:42.846 --> 44:45.265
But now, I'm rather tempted to do so.

44:46.642 --> 44:48.936
I'll take that as a no.

44:49.019 --> 44:50.771
Lower your knife so we can talk.

44:50.854 --> 44:53.273
Why don't you lower your gun first
before you ask?

44:53.357 --> 44:54.650
Okay, fine.

44:56.068 --> 44:59.571
Let's both lower our weapons
on the count of three.

45:00.823 --> 45:01.657
Now.

45:02.366 --> 45:03.200
One.

45:04.618 --> 45:05.452
Two.

45:07.788 --> 45:08.872
Three.

45:13.252 --> 45:15.379
I see that you don't trust me.

45:15.462 --> 45:17.172
I could say the same about you.

45:17.923 --> 45:19.049
Are you a hitman?

45:19.133 --> 45:21.385
You must have led quite a shady life

45:22.136 --> 45:24.221
to keep fearing for your life like that.

45:24.304 --> 45:26.181
We live in such times, do we not?

45:27.141 --> 45:29.893
You can't survive
without committing a crime.

45:30.644 --> 45:34.148
And even the innocent can die
for all sorts of reasons.

45:59.506 --> 46:01.008
What do you want from me?

46:01.091 --> 46:03.218
I heard that you're Mr. Omniscient.

46:03.302 --> 46:06.680
Then you must know that my prices vary
depending on the information.

46:07.264 --> 46:11.894
It's quite the range of prices
from high to low-level information.

46:12.478 --> 46:13.729
I'm looking for someone.

46:14.480 --> 46:15.397
He's Japanese.

46:16.064 --> 46:17.733
- Occupation?
- A painter.

46:18.317 --> 46:22.821
Unless he's a soldier or a high official,
his information is considered low-level.

46:22.905 --> 46:25.657
Unfortunately,
I don't deal with low-level information.

46:26.408 --> 46:29.453
It takes too much work
and barely makes any money.

46:29.536 --> 46:30.996
Sachimoto is his name.

46:31.955 --> 46:34.666
- I don't know him.
- He's in his mid-30s.

46:35.417 --> 46:36.251
No clue.

46:36.335 --> 46:41.131
He wasn't fluent in Joseon tongue,
which means he hadn't been here for long.

46:41.215 --> 46:42.591
I still haven't got a clue.

46:51.099 --> 46:53.936
I'm looking for my mother
who went missing ten years ago.

47:00.275 --> 47:01.443
So,

47:02.194 --> 47:04.279
Sachimoto must be the lover
she ran away with.

47:04.863 --> 47:05.697
What?

47:05.781 --> 47:08.784
Ten years is quite a long time.

47:08.867 --> 47:11.453
If she's started a new family,
it might be best not to look for--

47:13.664 --> 47:14.998
Rude bastard.

47:16.542 --> 47:20.087
Your crude words tell me
that you're not Mr. Omniscient,

47:21.296 --> 47:23.131
but Mr. Trash of this city.

47:28.512 --> 47:31.765
Well, I won't deny it.

47:33.100 --> 47:34.893
I was born trash,

47:34.977 --> 47:38.730
and I've lived a trashy
and desperate life to get here.

47:40.524 --> 47:41.859
Watch that mouth of yours.

47:43.277 --> 47:46.029
Your vain words
will lead you to die in vain.

47:48.532 --> 47:50.033
What's your name?

47:59.376 --> 48:01.086
You have quite beautiful eyes.

48:11.430 --> 48:12.848
Are you taunting me?

48:15.893 --> 48:18.228
Should I pluck your eyes out?

48:22.482 --> 48:24.318
Either way, it was nice meeting you.

48:26.236 --> 48:27.237
You're crazy.

48:34.912 --> 48:35.996
Till we meet again.

48:42.753 --> 48:44.630
She's looking for Sachimoto?

48:46.924 --> 48:48.091
Sachimoto…

49:31.468 --> 49:33.720
Mr. Sachimoto, you have been summoned.

50:19.349 --> 50:22.269
What's the occasion, my friend?
You rarely send word to me.

50:26.773 --> 50:29.109
Do you know where that girl Myeong-ja is?

50:29.943 --> 50:31.361
Myeong-ja?

50:31.445 --> 50:33.030
Myeong-ja, Myeong…

50:35.532 --> 50:37.534
The cheeky courtesan
from Spring Moon Hall?

50:39.703 --> 50:42.831
She once professed her love for me
while in my arms.

50:44.082 --> 50:47.836
But then she became Ishikawa's mistress
and broke my heart.

50:47.919 --> 50:49.588
Why are you asking me?

50:51.465 --> 50:54.634
It's been a week since she disappeared.
You didn't know?

50:54.718 --> 50:58.180
I know she's gone missing,
but I don't know where she is, silly.

51:01.183 --> 51:04.519
Why? Did you think I kidnapped her
and hid her away?

51:08.315 --> 51:09.232
So you don't know.

51:10.442 --> 51:11.526
Why not

51:12.569 --> 51:14.654
take this chance
to put your money to good use?

51:15.739 --> 51:17.074
I heard the news.

51:17.783 --> 51:19.868
You're going to lose it all
to Ishikawa anyway.

51:19.951 --> 51:23.121
Wouldn't it be nice to spend it
on our patriotic comrades?

51:23.872 --> 51:25.624
You will get to be a patriot,

51:25.707 --> 51:28.001
and our comrades will gain
a wealthy benefactor.

51:34.549 --> 51:36.259
Who said I'm going to lose it?

51:37.427 --> 51:39.554
I just have to find the girl, that's all.

51:40.222 --> 51:43.225
If she could be found,
Ishikawa would have found her already.

51:44.184 --> 51:47.187
It's been a week,
but there's still no sign of her.

51:47.270 --> 51:48.772
That's why he dragged you in.

51:51.316 --> 51:53.401
But I'm sure you know that already.

51:57.072 --> 51:58.073
You're drunk.

51:58.782 --> 51:59.991
You should go home.

52:00.826 --> 52:04.538
You may have earned your money like a dog,
but don't you spend it like one!

52:09.960 --> 52:11.128
If money

52:12.671 --> 52:15.340
cannot be used to help someone,
let alone be spent,

52:17.008 --> 52:19.094
it'll be nothing but a pile of dust.

52:20.178 --> 52:22.347
Don't obsess over the meaningless.

52:23.223 --> 52:26.059
I earned my money like a dog,
so I can spend it like one too.

52:26.560 --> 52:30.480
I put my life on the line to earn it.
Can't I spend it however I want?

52:30.564 --> 52:32.816
Do you have no place for Joseon
in your heart?

52:33.525 --> 52:35.569
No desire to do something for our country?

52:35.652 --> 52:38.113
I've never known the kind of Joseon
without Japan!

52:38.864 --> 52:42.742
I was born without a father and a country.
What do you want me to do about it?

52:44.494 --> 52:46.496
It's fine if you insult me,

52:47.664 --> 52:49.082
but don't insult my money.

52:51.001 --> 52:54.462
I may have worked like a dog to earn it,
but it means something to me.

52:55.088 --> 52:57.757
I don't care if it's a pile of dust
or a pile of crap.

52:58.258 --> 53:02.679
My money and fortune made me who I am,
and they keep me safe even now. Got that?

53:20.989 --> 53:24.159
I was just about to head home.
Can you give me a ride?

53:37.422 --> 53:38.506
Come in.

53:44.304 --> 53:46.139
Test Subject One is showing symptoms.

53:55.106 --> 53:56.775
It's faster than usual.

53:56.858 --> 53:58.151
Would you like to see it?

54:02.489 --> 54:03.907
Help me.

54:05.367 --> 54:06.910
My head…

54:08.453 --> 54:10.455
Please help me.

54:11.623 --> 54:13.959
My head is aching so much!

54:15.543 --> 54:16.878
It hurts so much!

54:18.088 --> 54:19.047
The serum?

54:20.423 --> 54:21.549
Not injected yet, sir.

54:31.059 --> 54:32.519
Another failure, then?

54:38.149 --> 54:39.359
What about Room Two?

54:41.236 --> 54:42.821
She has been quiet so far.

54:43.655 --> 54:44.739
What should we do?

54:45.448 --> 54:46.700
Shall I inject the serum?

54:48.910 --> 54:49.869
Proceed.

54:51.037 --> 54:51.997
Yes, sir.

55:22.485 --> 55:23.820
You've returned.

55:23.903 --> 55:26.072
Mrs. Nawol. You're still here?

55:26.156 --> 55:29.034
Actually, I have been waiting for you.

55:29.117 --> 55:33.330
The broker introduced me
to these people called sleuths.

55:33.913 --> 55:37.459
Apparently, they are experts
in finding missing people.

56:07.906 --> 56:11.534
So, how exactly do you find
the missing people?

56:12.452 --> 56:14.287
It depends on the situation.

56:14.371 --> 56:17.374
But I'm sure there's a process
that works particularly well.

56:17.957 --> 56:21.336
A secret method or special approach
that only you know…

56:21.419 --> 56:22.253
Nothing?

56:23.880 --> 56:25.548
We do not give up.

56:26.132 --> 56:29.094
We don't give up on the person
that needs to be found.

56:29.177 --> 56:33.681
Our method is to track them persistently
to the ends of the earth.

56:36.976 --> 56:38.645
How many have you found that way?

56:38.728 --> 56:41.272
If we don't seem reliable,
you can find someone else.

56:43.274 --> 56:45.735
I'm about to entrust you
with a serious task.

56:45.819 --> 56:48.071
It's only right for me
to perform a simple check.

56:48.154 --> 56:51.116
We aren't interested enough
to put up with such a thing.

56:51.199 --> 56:56.371
We have taken more than 200 cases
over the past ten years.

56:57.080 --> 57:01.084
Of those, we have found about 140.

57:01.167 --> 57:02.335
Including the dead.

57:02.419 --> 57:04.671
You don't have to answer his questions.

57:04.754 --> 57:07.090
He's not Mr. Omniscient of Gyeongseong.

57:08.007 --> 57:09.092
He's Mr. Trash.

57:09.175 --> 57:10.468
Chae-ok.

57:10.552 --> 57:12.220
I refuse to work for such a man.

57:14.180 --> 57:16.099
Just what did you do?

57:17.642 --> 57:18.726
I didn't do anything.

57:19.978 --> 57:22.772
All I said was that her eyes

57:24.441 --> 57:26.734
were quite beautiful.

57:27.402 --> 57:29.654
- Pardon?
- Let's go, Chae-ok.

57:31.948 --> 57:33.408
Sachimoto, you said?

57:35.285 --> 57:36.494
A Japanese man.

57:37.412 --> 57:40.081
A painter in his mid-30s.

57:41.124 --> 57:43.877
I thought you didn't deal
with low-level information.

57:46.671 --> 57:48.590
In principle, I don't.

57:48.673 --> 57:50.550
But the situation calls for it.

57:50.633 --> 57:55.013
If it changes depending on the situation,
that's an anomaly, not a principle.

57:55.096 --> 57:58.558
Let's call it flexibility
in dealing with urgent situations.

57:58.641 --> 58:00.435
Maybe you're just being crafty?

58:00.518 --> 58:01.895
That's how desperate I am.

58:01.978 --> 58:03.897
You're also that pathetic, you know that?

58:06.357 --> 58:07.984
In this city,

58:09.152 --> 58:12.071
I'm the man to talk to
for Japanese connections.

58:12.155 --> 58:14.824
Be it Government-General officials,
businessmen,

58:14.908 --> 58:16.743
doctors, or judges…

58:17.827 --> 58:20.246
I have connections to anyone, anywhere.

58:20.330 --> 58:22.790
If you have that many connections
and information,

58:24.083 --> 58:27.420
you can find Myeong-ja
of Spring Moon Hall on your own.

58:28.546 --> 58:29.923
If she's still alive, that is.

58:31.508 --> 58:34.219
Most times, when I pull this many strings,

58:34.302 --> 58:37.472
any kind of lead will surface
within half a day.

58:38.806 --> 58:40.934
But since I haven't heard anything so far…

58:41.017 --> 58:42.936
Do you think she might be dead?

58:43.603 --> 58:45.605
Whatever the case, please find her.

58:45.688 --> 58:48.608
In the meantime, I will ask around
for information on Sachimoto.

58:48.691 --> 58:51.945
You don't have to.
We'll take care of our own business.

58:53.154 --> 58:54.989
Aren't you looking for your mother?

59:02.664 --> 59:04.249
I'm sure I can be of help.

59:05.458 --> 59:06.459
I guarantee it.

59:08.169 --> 59:09.837
Let me ask you one thing.

59:12.799 --> 59:16.052
Are you a good man or a bad man?

59:24.727 --> 59:25.937
I'm just…

59:28.273 --> 59:30.858
a man who is determined to survive.

59:38.032 --> 59:39.617
How much time can you give us?

59:40.785 --> 59:41.911
Father.

59:44.080 --> 59:47.208
Until the cherry blossoms fall.

01:00:11.899 --> 01:00:14.527
What do I need to draw today?

01:00:14.611 --> 01:00:15.945
Go to Room Two.

01:00:17.905 --> 01:00:20.617
You may step closer for a better look.

01:00:24.078 --> 01:00:25.622
But don't get too close.

01:00:27.498 --> 01:00:29.167
It could be dangerous.

01:00:31.002 --> 01:00:31.836
Yes, sir.

01:00:58.655 --> 01:01:01.658
Excuse me.
Can I shine a light for a moment?
